      <p class="_abstract">Starting in Compliance Operator 1.9.0, add labels and annotations to <code>Rule</code> and <code>CustomRule</code> objects so matching metadata is displayed on <code>ComplianceCheckResult</code> objects after a scan. Downstream tools, dashboards, and ticketing workflows can use this metadata without maintaining a separate mapping.</p>
      <h2 id="compliance-operator-checkresult-custom-metadata-overview_compliance-operator-checkresult-metadata" class="group scroll-mt-20">Understanding custom metadata on rules and check results<a href="#compliance-operator-checkresult-custom-metadata-overview_compliance-operator-checkresult-metadata" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When the Compliance Operator creates or updates a <code>ComplianceCheckResult</code> object for a check that Open Security Content Automation Protocol (OpenSCAP) evaluates, it copies custom labels and annotations from the corresponding <code>Rule</code> object in the same namespace.</p>
